{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790314446,"nonce":"9yXGvgLF4EF5RS+gt+OJIrmT8Hw=","title":"Tier-0 first compile of loop-free functions slows crypto_pyaes, scimark_montecarlo and scimark_lu","message":"63916738 \"Tiered: a stub compiles a loop-free function's body as lowered first\" is where crypto_pyaes and scimark_montecarlo step up on the NUC; the parent f1b9940a runs them at base speed. The slow runs are the common case but not every run: a minority land at base speed, so which code the hot calls end up running looks timing dependent (the optimised replacement not reaching every caller, or reaching it late).\n\nNUC x86_64, release llvm-backend, ZYPY_LLVM=1, speed kernels staged as run.py stages them (--fast trials), interleaved rounds, mean iteration ms, median (min..max):\n- crypto_pyaes -n 5: base 678f49eb 161.8 (157.4..176.2), f1b9940a 159.9 (153.8..163.6), 63916738 217.2 (206.7..220.5), 5a6d14fd 210.0 (209.2..211.0). Whole-process wall 902 to 1147 ms.\n- scimark_montecarlo: base 82.8 (76.4..102.2), f1b9940a 77.8 (76.1..83.7), 63916738 111.8 (109.6..115.1), 5a6d14fd 95 to 113. Mac arm64 (under load): base 67.6, 5a6d14fd 86.3.\n- scimark_lu: gradual, base 4249, 05fdc099 4322, f1b9940a 4448, 63916738 4696, 5a6d14fd 4712 to 4744 ms. Mac: 3986 to 4242.\n\nSmaller, same range: meteor-contest wall +4 to 7% from the inliner package (717bf598..05fdc099: base 491.7, 05fdc099 516.8 ms wall on the NUC).\n\nJSON under the perf-designs wave1_measure directory (nuc_speed*, bis1/bis2 on the NUC at ~/wt/w1m).","files":null}]}